# Cross-file dependencies

RulePackVersion: 1.0.0
Mode: sniff-system

## MUST

- Respect the stated load or init order in the architecture manifest when one is provided.
- Flag circular initialization or mutual construction between peer systems.
- One clear owner per shared mutable concern across the audited files.
- Do not reach upward from a lower-layer scene or system into a higher-layer owner when the manifest defines layers.
- Domain or core logic must not depend on UI types across the audited set.

## Audit focus

1. Manifest load-order or responsibility violations
2. Circular init or wiring between files
3. Split ownership of the same concern across files
4. Layer or scene direction violations (lower depending on higher)
5. Hidden static mutable coupling across the set

## Guidance

- Prefer findings that name the files involved.
- If no manifest is provided, still flag clear circular or layer violations; do not invent a preferred architecture.
